      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The diagonal of a rectangular prism can be found using the 3D distance formula, which is derived from the Pythagorean Theorem in three dimensions. The formula is:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2 + (z_2 - z_1)^2} \\]\nwhere \\((x_1, y_1, z_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2, z_2)\\) are the coordinates of the two points in space.\n\nIn this problem, the rectangular prism has dimensions 10 inches by 20 inches by 10 inches. The diagonal connecting points \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) can be represented as follows:\n- Point \\(A\\) is at \\((0, 1, 0)\\)\n- Point \\(B\\) is at \\((20, 1, 10)\\)\n\nLet's use the 3D distance formula to calculate the length of the diagonal:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(20 - 0)^2 + (1 - 1)^2 + (10 - 0)^2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{20^2 + 0^2 + 10^2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{400 + 0 + 100} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{500} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{100 \\times 5} \\]\n\\[ d = 10\\sqrt{5} \\]\n\nTherefore, the length of the diagonal connecting point \\(A\\) and point \\(B\\) is \\(\\boxed{10\\sqrt{5}}\\) inches.",
